{"id": "Dd8rQppTP53", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Maa Shailputri hold a trishul AND a lotus? 🔱🪷 A weapon in one hand, a flower in the other, and the reason is beautiful. (Part 2)\n\n🔱 The trishul protects. Its three prongs are the past, the present and the future, and she guards all three.\n🪷 The lotus grows out of mud, yet not a drop sticks to it: stay pure, even in a messy world.\n\nStrength without calm is scary. Calm without strength gets pushed around. She carries both: strong enough to protect, soft enough to love. That’s why Navratri begins with her.\n\n📚 Her whole story is in Book 1 of our Navadurga picture books for ages 4–8. Books 1–3 are out: Set of 3 for ₹600 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n👇 Which do you need today: TRISHUL or LOTUS? Tell us in the comments. Save this for Navratri, and send it to someone who is both. Follow for Part 3: why Brahmacharini gave up food.\n\n#navratri #shailputri #navadurga #maadurga #navratri2026 trishul lotus hindumythology indianmythology mythologyforkids picturebooks kidsbooks booksforkids sanatandharma rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1790850043, "like_count": 1229, "comment_count": 19, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1146853141025549a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 44.431, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPPk6Mbw2b4oK5cOHvU2uCkfNSwF7yKoLFoNAP89JmYP12ZkNMxp71yO00flYjWcO35czAI4qB5AqLvAYmpe8Y8usHHqfDFm2cJ3cs.mp4?_nc_cat=109&_nc_oc=AdpfTbG1Vmd4Tf2C9z2luefXE-ESnnSOUcWfMf5zDgDvrrdpg1SlgBOyi5Yxcdgj3-shCiYzDN5j9odeWDmbFKbr&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=1exRkyrMUHQQ7kNvwFyn-Hl&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=OPJBEMDCXMzoAPjt1BR5Vg&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQTynXDUUCRdWfwW6Th